update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_privacy$<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><div class="muted">How QuotesDone Technologies collects, uses, shares and protects personal data on the QuotesDone anonymous quotation marketplace, and your rights under UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (the Personal Data Protection Law).</div><div class="card"><h2>1. Who We Are (Data Controller)</h2><p>This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your personal data when you use QuotesDone, an online B2B anonymous quotation marketplace.</p><p>The data controller is:</p><ul><li>QuotesDone Technologies, a Dubai Sole Establishment</li><li>DET Dubai Trader License No. 1633275</li><li>Owner: Ahmad Mhd Nabil Alzain</li><li>Address: Dubai, United Arab Emirates</li><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com; Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (the number on our licence record is +971 56 791 8605)</li></ul><p>We process personal data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (PDPL), and its implementing regime overseen by the UAE Data Office, which from June 2026 operates within the new UAE Federal Authority for Artificial Intelligence and Data. This policy applies to customers, suppliers and visitors. Where you act on behalf of a business, references to your personal data mean the personal data of the individuals concerned.</p><h2>2. Personal Data We Collect</h2><p>Depending on how you use the platform, we collect:</p><ul><li>Customer identity and contact data: your name, email address and mobile number, with the mobile number verified by one-time password (OTP).</li><li>Request content: the job or request you submit as text, voice recordings, photographs or drawings, including any personal data you choose to include.</li><li>Supplier data: business details and Know Your Customer (KYC) documents provided for vetting and onboarding.</li><li>Payment data: a payment reference returned by our payment processor, Stripe. We do not store full card numbers; card and Apple Pay details are handled by Stripe, which is certified to the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS).</li><li>Usage and technical data: logs, device and connection information, and records of platform activity.</li></ul><p>We do not intentionally collect special categories of data. Please avoid including sensitive details in request content unless necessary.</p><h2>3. Purposes and Lawful Bases</h2><p>We process personal data for clear purposes, each supported by a lawful basis under the PDPL:</p><ul><li>To create and manage your account, verify your mobile by OTP, and provide the marketplace, including matching requests to suppliers and enabling paid reveals (performance of a contract).</li><li>To calculate and collect the customer Reveal Fee of 3% of the quoted value at the point you choose to reveal a supplier, and to keep accounting records (performance of a contract and legal obligation). Suppliers pay no commission or success fee on jobs they win.</li><li>To vet suppliers and verify KYC documents, prevent fraud and misuse, secure the platform and improve our services (legitimate interests).</li><li>To share a chosen supplier&#x27;s contact details on a paid reveal, and for optional marketing (your consent, which you may withdraw at any time).</li></ul><p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, we balance these against your rights and interests.</p><h2>4. Smart and Automated Processing</h2><p>QuotesDone uses smart and automated tools to operate the marketplace. These tools:</p><ul><li>Structure and standardise the requests you submit (including converting voice, photos and drawings into a structured brief).</li><li>Match each request to vetted suppliers likely to be able to quote.</li><li>Summarise requests and quotes to make them easier to compare.</li></ul><p>This automated processing supports our service but does not produce binding legal effects on you without human involvement, and you remain free to accept, reject or ignore any quote. You may contact us to ask questions about, or object to, automated processing as described in the Your Rights section. Where automated processing could significantly affect individuals, we assess its impact before deploying it.</p><h2>5. How We Share Data</h2><p>Anonymity is central to QuotesDone. We share personal data only as follows:</p><ul><li>Request content is shared with matched suppliers WITHOUT revealing your identity, so suppliers can prepare anonymised quotes.</li><li>Your contact details are disclosed to a single supplier only after you pay the Reveal Fee and consent to the reveal for that chosen supplier; suppliers receive customer contact data only for jobs revealed to them.</li><li>Our payment processor, Stripe, receives the data needed to take payment (card or Apple Pay) and returns a payment reference.</li><li>Service providers (such as hosting, communications and analytics) process data on our behalf under written instructions.</li></ul><p>We may also disclose data where required by UAE law, a court of competent authority, or to protect our legal rights. We do not sell personal data.</p><h2>6. Cross-Border Transfers</h2><p>Some of our service providers may process personal data outside the United Arab Emirates. Where this happens, we apply the safeguards required by Articles 22 and 23 of the PDPL.</p><ul><li>We transfer data to countries the UAE Data Office recognises as providing an adequate level of protection; or</li><li>Where adequacy is not established, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as contractual clauses obliging the recipient to protect the data to UAE standards, or on your explicit consent, in each case in a manner that does not conflict with the public and security interests of the State.</li></ul><p>You may contact us for more information about the specific safeguards applied to a transfer.</p><h2>7. Data Retention</h2><p>We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described above and to meet legal obligations.</p><ul><li>Account data is kept while your account is active and for a reasonable period afterwards.</li><li>Request content is retained to operate and improve matching, then deleted or anonymised when no longer needed.</li><li>Transaction and financial records, including Reveal Fee and registration-fee records, are retained for the periods required by UAE accounting and tax law.</li><li>Supplier KYC documents are retained for the duration of the relationship and any legally required period thereafter.</li><li>Logs are kept for limited periods for security and audit purposes.</li></ul><p>When a retention period ends, we securely delete or irreversibly anonymise the data. Our internal Data Protection and Retention Policy sets out the detailed schedule.</p><h2>8. Your Rights Under the PDPL</h2><p>Subject to the conditions and exceptions in the PDPL, you have the right to:</p><ul><li>Access your personal data and obtain information about how it is processed.</li><li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li><li>Request deletion of your data where the legal grounds apply.</li><li>Object to, or request restriction of, certain processing, including processing based on legitimate interests and certain automated processing.</li><li>Request that your personal data be provided to you, or transferred to another controller, in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format (data portability), where technically feasible.</li><li>Request that your data be transferred to you or another controller in a structured format, where applicable.</li><li>Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal.</li></ul><p>To exercise any right, contact us at management@quotesdone.com. We will respond within the timeframes required by the PDPL. If you are not satisfied, you may lodge a complaint with the UAE Data Office.</p><h2>9. Electronic Marketing and Communications</h2><p>We send transactional messages you need to use the service — for example mobile one-time passwords (OTP), request and quote notifications, and account or payment confirmations — on the basis of our contract with you; these are not marketing.</p><p>We send marketing or promotional messages by email, SMS or other electronic means only where you have given consent, and you can withdraw consent or unsubscribe at any time using the link or instructions in the message, or by emailing management@quotesdone.com. We handle electronic communications in line with the UAE telecommunications and electronic-marketing rules overseen by the Telecommunications and Digital Government Regulatory Authority (TDRA) and the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021). We do not sell your contact details for third-party marketing.</p><h2>10. Security</h2><p>We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, alteration or disclosure, consistent with the PDPL and the Electronic Transactions and Trust Services Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021.</p><ul><li>Access to personal data is restricted to authorised personnel on a need-to-know basis.</li><li>We use encryption in transit, OTP verification for customer mobile numbers, and segregation of anonymised request content from identity data.</li><li>Payment card data is handled by Stripe, our PCI DSS–certified payment processor, and is not stored by us.</li></ul><p>No system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. If a personal data breach occurs that meets the legal threshold, we will notify the UAE Data Office and affected individuals as required by the PDPL.</p><h2>11. Children, Changes and Contact</h2><p>QuotesDone is a business-to-business platform intended for users aged 18 and over. It is not directed at minors, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a minor has provided us data, please contact us so we can delete it.</p><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our services or the law. The current version is always available on our platform, and material changes will be notified where appropriate.</p><p>For any privacy question, to exercise your rights, or to reach our data protection contact, please use:</p><ul><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com</li><li>Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (licence record: +971 56 791 8605)</li><li>Post: QuotesDone Technologies, Dubai, United Arab Emirates (our DET Trader License is for an online business with no shop front, so there is no street address)</li></ul><p>This policy is governed by the laws of the UAE, and disputes are subject to the courts of Dubai.</p></div>$qd_privacy$
 where slug = 'privacy';
update public.legal_documents set version = '1.5', effective_date = date '2026-09-23',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'privacy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_cookie_policy$<h1>Cookie Policy</h1><div class="muted">How QuotesDone uses cookies and similar technologies, how we obtain consent consistent with UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021, and how you can manage or disable them.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Cookie Policy explains how QuotesDone Technologies (DET Dubai Trader License No. 1633275) uses cookies and similar technologies on the QuotesDone platform. It should be read together with our Privacy Policy.</p><p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. Similar technologies include local storage, pixels and tags that perform comparable functions.</p><p>Where cookies collect or relate to personal data, we handle that data in accordance with the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (PDPL). This policy tells you which cookies we use, why, and how you can control them. By using the platform after being shown our cookie notice, and where required after giving consent, you agree to the use of cookies as described here.</p><h2>2. Cookies We Use</h2><p>We use the following categories:</p><ul><li>Essential and session cookies: necessary to run the platform, keep you signed in, remember your request as you build it, and enable core features such as paid reveals. The platform cannot function properly without these.</li><li>Security cookies: help us verify sessions, support OTP-based mobile verification, detect fraud and protect the platform and your account.</li><li>First-visit link tags (local storage, not a cookie; key qd-first-touch): when you first arrive through one of our own links, the campaign tags in that link (for example utm_source=linkedin and the name of the post), the page you landed on and when you arrived. It holds no identifier and nothing about you, and it never leaves your device unless you register as a supplier, when it is sent with your registration so that we know which post brought you. Clearing this site&#x27;s data in your browser removes it.</li></ul><p>We set no analytics, advertising or other non-essential cookies, and we do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or to sell your data. If that ever changes, this policy will be updated and your consent asked for before any such cookie is set.</p><h2>3. Consent Approach</h2><p>Our approach to cookie consent is consistent with the PDPL:</p><ul><li>Essential and security cookies are strictly necessary for the service and are set without requiring separate consent, because they are required to deliver the service you request.</li><li>We set no non-essential cookies. If we ever introduce analytics or any other non-essential cookie, we will ask for your consent through the cookie notice before it is set, and you will be free to decline or to change your mind at any time.</li></ul><p>Because only essential and security cookies are in use, there is no non-essential category to decline, and no core feature of QuotesDone depends on that choice.</p><h2>4. Managing and Disabling Cookies</h2><p>You can control cookies in several ways:</p><ul><li>Read the cookie notice shown on your first visit. It records that you have seen it; there is no non-essential category to switch off, because none is set.</li><li>Adjust your browser settings to block or delete cookies, or to warn you before cookies are stored. Most browsers allow this through their privacy or settings menu.</li><li>Use your device or browser&#x27;s controls for local storage and similar technologies.</li></ul><p>Please note that blocking essential or security cookies may stop parts of the platform from working, including sign-in, request submission and paid reveals.</p><p>For help managing cookies, contact us at management@quotesdone.com.</p><h2>5. Third-Party Tags</h2><p>Some cookies and tags are set by third parties that provide services to us:</p><ul><li>Our payment processor, Stripe, which may set cookies or use similar technologies to process card and Apple Pay payments securely and to prevent payment fraud during the reveal and payment flows.</li></ul><p>These third parties process data under their own terms and policies and, where they act for us, under written instructions. We share only what is needed for the relevant service. We encourage you to review the privacy and cookie notices of any third-party services you interact with through the platform.</p><h2>6. Changes and Contact</h2><p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the technologies we use or in applicable law. The current version is always available on our platform, and the effective date will be updated when we make changes.</p><p>If you have any questions about our use of cookies or wish to exercise your data protection rights under the PDPL, please contact:</p><ul><li>QuotesDone Technologies</li><li>Email: management@quotesdone.com</li><li>Phone: +971 50 931 9355 (licence record: +971 56 791 8605)</li><li>Address: Dubai, United Arab Emirates</li></ul><p>This policy is governed by the laws of the UAE, and any disputes are subject to the courts of Dubai.</p></div>$qd_cookie_policy$
 where slug = 'cookie-policy';
update public.legal_documents set version = '1.4', effective_date = date '2026-09-23',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'cookie-policy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_refund_policy$<h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1><div class="muted">Explains when the QuotesDone Reveal Fee is and is not refundable, how to request a refund, processing times and method, supplier registration-fee terms, and your preserved statutory rights under UAE Federal Law No. 15 of 2020.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy applies to QuotesDone, an online business-to-business quotation marketplace operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; DET Dubai Trader License No. 1633275), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>QuotesDone is a marketplace and facilitator only. We connect customers with suppliers and provide anonymised quotations. We are not a contractor, supplier or party to the works quoted, and this Policy governs only the fees you pay to QuotesDone, not amounts payable to a supplier under any separate contract you enter into.</p><p>This Policy must be read together with our Terms &amp; Conditions. It is governed by the laws of the UAE and applied without prejudice to your non-waivable statutory rights under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023).</p><h2>2. The Reveal Fee</h2><p>To unlock the identity and contact details of a chosen supplier behind an anonymised quotation, you pay a Reveal Fee equal to 3% of the quoted amount, and nothing more: no card fee or surcharge is added. No cap applies to the Reveal Fee. Both amounts and the total are shown to you before you pay. QuotesDone is not registered for VAT, and no VAT is charged on either.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is a charge for the reveal service provided by QuotesDone. They are separate from, and additional to, any price agreed between you and the supplier for the actual goods, services or works.</p><p>Because the Reveal Fee unlocks supplier information immediately on payment, it is generally treated as earned once the reveal is delivered, subject to the specific refund right described below and to your statutory rights under UAE law.</p><h2>3. When a Reveal Is Refunded</h2><p>We refund everything you paid for a reveal in one defined circumstance: where a revealed supplier does not respond to you within five (5) working days of your payment and does not respond to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO&#39;s final call. You do not need to prove anything for the clock to start: we track every reveal from the moment you pay. If the supplier has not responded within three (3) working days, we chase the supplier on your behalf and copy you; if there is still no response on the fifth (5th) working day, the case goes to QuotesDone&#39;s CEO for a final call; if the supplier does not respond to that call, the refund is issued.</p><p>If you have tried to reach the supplier yourself, dated copies of emails, messages sent through the Platform, or call logs help us close the case faster, but they are not a condition of the refund. Working days are Monday to Friday, excluding UAE public holidays.</p><p>If these conditions are met, everything you paid to reveal that supplier is refunded: the Reveal Fee. The CEO&#39;s decision, whichever way it goes, is recorded against your refund case reference and the decision reference, and both are shown to you in your account and quoted when we confirm the outcome. This refund right is in addition to any remedy available to you under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection.</p><h2>4. When a Reveal Is Not Refunded</h2><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable once the revealed supplier has responded to you within the five-working-day window, as the reveal service has then been fully delivered and the supplier has engaged.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable for a change of mind, for example where you decide not to proceed with a supplier who did respond, where you select a different supplier, or where the supplier&#x27;s pricing or terms no longer suit you.</p><p>The Reveal Fee is not refundable where the supplier responded to you or to QuotesDone within the five-working-day window. Nothing in this section limits your non-waivable rights under UAE consumer protection law where they apply.</p><h2>5. How to Request a Refund</h2><p>You do not need to submit a request for a non-response refund: the ladder above runs automatically from the moment you pay. You can still tell us at any time that the supplier is not responding, by emailing management@quotesdone.com or by using the support function on the Platform, and we will chase the supplier immediately.</p><p>If you do write to us, your account email and the reveal reference are enough. Proof of your own attempts to reach the supplier (emails, Platform messages or call logs) is optional: it can help us close the case faster, but it is never a condition of the refund (see section 3).</p><p>We may ask for further information to identify your reveal. Providing complete and accurate information helps us assess and process eligible refunds promptly.</p><h2>6. Processing Time and Method</h2><p>Once QuotesDone&#39;s CEO decides a refund, it is issued to the original payment method through our payment processor, Stripe, and we confirm it to you with your refund case reference. Banks and card issuers usually take seven (7) to fourteen (14) working days to show the refund on your statement.</p><p><b>Payments handled by Stripe · PCI DSS.</b> Your card or Apple Pay payment is processed by Stripe, a payment processor certified to the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard; QuotesDone never sees or stores your full card number.</p><p>Refunds are made in the currency of the original payment and for everything you paid for the reveal: the Reveal Fee. QuotesDone deducts nothing from your refund and never passes the payment processor&#39;s costs to you. What QuotesDone recovers under the Supplier Agreement (the amount refunded to you, the payment processor&#39;s fee on your payment that QuotesDone could not recover, an administrative fee of AED 500, and interest at 12% per annum, or the lower amounts of the version of the Supplier Agreement the supplier had signed) is charged to the supplier whose non-response caused the refund, never to you.</p><p>If a refund cannot be returned to the original payment method for reasons outside our control, we will agree an alternative lawful method with you.</p><h2>7. Supplier Registration-Fee Terms</h2><p>Suppliers may be charged a registration fee to join and maintain a profile on the Platform. QuotesDone charges suppliers no commission, success fee or transaction fee on jobs they win. These terms apply to suppliers, not to customers.</p><p>Any supplier registration fee is charged for access to the marketplace and listing services over the registration period. Where a fee covers a defined period, it is generally non-refundable for the unused portion once access has been granted, except where required by law or expressly agreed in writing.</p><h2>8. Your Statutory Rights</h2><p>Nothing in this Policy excludes, restricts or waives any right you may have under Federal Law No. 15 of 2020 on Consumer Protection and its Implementing Regulation (Cabinet Resolution No. 66 of 2023), or under other applicable UAE law.</p><p>Where a service is not provided as described, your statutory remedies under UAE consumer protection law continue to apply alongside the contractual refund right in this Policy.</p><p>If you believe your consumer rights have not been honoured, you may contact us first and, if unresolved, escalate to the relevant authority as set out in our Complaints &amp; Dispute Resolution Policy.</p></div>$qd_refund_policy$
 where slug = 'refund-policy';
update public.legal_documents set version = '1.8', effective_date = date '2026-09-24',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'refund-policy';

update public.legal_documents set body_html = $qd_acceptable_use$<h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1><div class="muted">Defines permitted and prohibited conduct on the QuotesDone Platform, including accuracy of information, prohibitions on fraud, abuse, scraping, circumvention, IP infringement and off-platform identification of suppliers before reveal, the consequences of breach, and how to report misuse.</div><div class="card"><h2>1. About This Policy</h2><p>This Acceptable Use Policy applies to all users of QuotesDone, operated by QuotesDone Technologies (Dubai Sole Establishment; DET Dubai Trader License No. 1633275), Dubai, United Arab Emirates.</p><p>By accessing or using the Platform, you agree to use it lawfully and in line with this Policy, our Terms &amp; Conditions and applicable UAE law.</p><p>This Policy supports the integrity of the anonymous-quotation model, which depends on accurate information and on supplier identities remaining protected until a Reveal Fee is paid.</p><h2>2. Permitted Conduct</h2><p>You may use QuotesDone to request, receive and compare anonymised quotations, to pay the applicable Reveal Fee to unlock a chosen supplier, and to communicate with suppliers for genuine, lawful business purposes.</p><p>You must provide accurate, current and complete information when registering, submitting requirements and requesting quotations, and keep your account details up to date.</p><p>You must keep your login credentials secure and are responsible for activity carried out under your account.</p><h2>3. Prohibited Conduct</h2><p>You must not use the Platform for any unlawful, fraudulent or deceptive purpose, submit false, misleading or fictitious requests or quotations, or impersonate any person or business.</p><p>You must not abuse, harass, threaten or defame other users or our staff, post unlawful, infringing or offensive content, or upload malware or anything that could harm the Platform or its users.</p><p>You must not infringe the intellectual property or other rights of QuotesDone or any third party, including by copying, reproducing or exploiting Platform content without authorisation.</p><h2>4. No Scraping or Circumvention</h2><p>You must not scrape, harvest, crawl, data-mine or use automated means to extract data from the Platform, nor attempt to access areas, accounts or data you are not authorised to access.</p><p>You must not interfere with or circumvent the security, anonymisation, payment or reveal mechanisms of the Platform, or take any action designed to avoid paying the Reveal Fee.</p><p>You must not reverse engineer, disrupt, overload or otherwise compromise the Platform&#x27;s normal operation.</p><h2>5. Protecting Supplier Anonymity</h2><p>The Platform anonymises supplier identities until you pay the Reveal Fee. You must not attempt to identify, contact or deal with a supplier off-platform before reveal, including by deducing or researching a supplier&#x27;s identity from a quotation.</p><p>You must not, after a reveal, deal with a supplier in a way designed to deprive QuotesDone of the Reveal Fee, such as deliberately taking a transaction off the Platform to avoid charges.</p><p>These rules protect the fairness of the marketplace for both customers and suppliers and form an essential condition of using the Platform.</p><h2>6. Consequences of Breach</h2><p>If you breach this Policy, we may, at our discretion and proportionate to the breach, issue a warning, restrict features, suspend or terminate your account, remove content, or withhold a reveal.</p><p>Serious or unlawful conduct, including fraud, circumvention of fees, intellectual property infringement or unlawful content, may result in legal action, the agreed compensation set out in the Terms of Service or the Supplier Agreement, and referral to the competent UAE authorities, including under the Cybercrime Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 34 of 2021).</p><p>We may retain and use relevant records as evidence to the extent permitted by Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data and other applicable UAE law.</p><h2>7. Reporting Misuse</h2><p>If you become aware of any breach of this Policy, suspected fraud, security vulnerability or other misuse of the Platform, please report it to us at management@quotesdone.com or through the Platform&#x27;s reporting function.</p><p>Please include enough detail to allow us to investigate, such as the accounts, quotations or messages involved and any supporting evidence.</p><p>We take reports seriously, investigate appropriately, and may cooperate with the competent UAE authorities where required by law.</p></div>$qd_acceptable_use$
 where slug = 'acceptable-use';
update public.legal_documents set version = '1.4', effective_date = date '2026-09-23',
       content_sha256 = encode(sha256(convert_to(body_html, 'UTF8')), 'hex'), updated_at = now()
 where slug = 'acceptable-use';
